Subject: Borrow Fusion For Argument Fields

What this does
  Adds OP_get_arg_field_nr: `get_arg(n) get_field(atom)` becomes one instruction
  that reads the receiver out of the argument register and never pushes it, so
  the js_dup / JS_FreeValue round trip on a known object and the 16-byte push and
  pop both disappear. It is the argument-register form of OP_get_loc_field_nr and
  shares that opcode's handler body through a register-file pointer; the encoding
  is identical, [atom:u32][arg:u16][ic:u16].

Why we need it
  The borrow fusion existed for locals only, so reading a property off a function
  parameter -- the shape of accessor-heavy and compiler-shaped code -- duplicated
  the receiver, freed it and pushed it for nothing. Measured here: 80,830
  executions on the real workload, 0.98% of its dispatches.

What it adds
  It takes the slot of OP_put_var_ref3, which put_short_code() had already made
  unreachable when it stopped synthesising the `OP_put_var_ref0 + idx` short
  forms, so no bytecode grows and no new guard is needed. The inline-cache site
  it carries is validated on read-back exactly like the local form's.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  Yes. `9999` carries the version and the rebuilt built-in blobs.

